THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE
====================

No third-party source code is vendored into this repository. The following are
runtime or build-time dependencies, obtained from their own distributions:

llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), MIT License.
  Cloned on the training pod to produce the GGUF exports. cloud/bootstrap.sh
  patches a local clone at build time to register this project's tokenizer hash
  in the BPE pre-tokenizer table. That patch is applied to their working copy on
  the pod and is not redistributed.

PyTorch, Hugging Face transformers, tokenizers and huggingface_hub are declared
in requirements.txt and are used as libraries under their respective licenses.


ARCHITECTURE AND PRIOR ART
==========================

The model in src/model/model.py is original code. It implements the Llama family
architecture (RoPE, RMSNorm, SwiGLU, grouped-query attention), which is a
published design rather than borrowed source. The implementation differs from
Meta's reference in substance as well as style, including a real-valued
split-half rotary embedding instead of the reference's complex-number
formulation.

Two conventions in the training code follow those popularised by Andrej
Karpathy's nanoGPT (MIT License): splitting AdamW parameter groups by tensor
rank for weight decay, and scaling residual-projection initialisation by
1/sqrt(2 * n_layers). These are short, widely reimplemented idioms rather than
copied code, and are credited here for completeness.
